    "body": "Thanks for the issue. You've used the template for bugs within the HTML standard, but this is a feature request. Please fill in the feature request template fully, as this helps us establish what ways this is solved today, for example.\n\nAs for the feature request itself, I think this might be better solved with things like css. We tend to avoid adding new presentational attributes in HTML, as it should be for semantics only. The width vs height of an element is presentational only, and offers no new semantics (e.g. accessible roles, focus traps, and so on).\n\nI'll leave this open for other vendors to comment on, but I think this should be closed as not planned. If no one disagrees then I propose we close it as such.",
